      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "spiritual_cleansing_ritual",
      "label": "Spiritual Cleansing Ritual",
      "description": "The practice of burning sage (smudging) is a traditional ritual used by Native American tribes and adopted by various spiritual and New Age communities for purification, cleansing negative energy, and promoting spiritual well-being. Understanding this ritual is essential to interpret the meme's intent, as the burning object is not merely a plant but a symbolic act with cultural and spiritual significance.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_17318fc4"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_5d464181",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "smudge_stick",
      "label": "Smudge Stick",
      "description": "A smudge stick is a bundle of dried herbs, most commonly sage, tied together and burned to release smoke for spiritual cleansing. This term is outside the image but necessary to understand the object being burned and its purpose. The text 'what's burning?' relies on the viewer knowing this object is a smudge stick to interpret the question as a reference to its ritual use.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_17318fc4"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_20ae9b04",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "ritualistic_smudging",
      "label": "Ritualistic Smudging",
      "description": "The act of smudging involves the intentional burning of sacred herbs to cleanse spaces, objects, or individuals. This practice is deeply rooted in indigenous traditions and has been adopted by various spiritual movements. The meme's rhetorical question 'what's burning?' implicitly references this ritualistic context, which requires external knowledge to fully appreciate the meme’s layered meaning.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_17318fc4"
